# strata-ui

These rules override style preference and third-party examples. Danilo owns product decisions. Cursor keeps Figma parity, types, tests, and this contract.

## Source code

- Zero comments in `.ts`, `.tsx`, and `.css`. `//` and `/* */` are forbidden.
- Strict TypeScript. `any`, implicit `any`, and assertions to `any` are forbidden.
- Polymorphism uses generics and Slot/`asChild`. Compound components expose named parts.

## Tests

- Vitest, React Testing Library, and vitest-axe.
- Test files are 100% in English: names, `describe`, `it`, labels, and messages.
- Cover keyboard, accessible name, visible focus, and axe with no violations.

## Figma, CSS, and TypeScript parity

- Canonical token name = the CSS custom property, including `--`.
- The Figma variable and the TypeScript literal use that same name. Public camelCase for tokens is forbidden.
- Figma variants use the TypeScript literals (`solid`, `outline`, `ghost`, `danger`, `sm`, `md`, `lg`, `rest`, `hover`, `active`, `focus-visible`, `disabled`).

## Accessibility

- Default theme: text, control borders, and the focus ring meet a minimum contrast of 7:1.
- Minimum target size of 44px CSS on interactive controls.
- Keyboard per APG: Tab, Shift+Tab, arrows, Enter, Space, Escape, Home, End.
- `:focus-visible` with a 2px ring, 2px offset, color `--color-focus-ring`.
- Complete ARIA. The accessible name is visible. Decorative icons are `aria-hidden`.
- Disabled uses `--color-fg-disabled` on `--color-bg-surface` or `--color-bg-canvas`, with no opacity fade.
- `--color-bg-muted` and `--color-bg-overlay` do not receive text.
